{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>And though he live a thousand years twice over</b>. This word is like ואילו לעבדים ולשפחות (Genesis 31:27). Some interpret it as a compound of אם and לו, and alef [multiplied] a thousand times, like עשרים פעמים הם ארבע מאות (twenty times is four hundred)." "<b>To one place.</b> That is, the grave."], :book :ecclesiastes, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {0 "The verse lemma here is Ecclesiastes 6:6, which reads ואף לו חיה אלפים שנים פעמים שתים; Ibn Ezra's comment addresses the word ואף, though he begins by citing ואלו, likely because he reads ואף לו as equivalent to ואלו."}, :source-witnesses [["Wikisource" "https://he.wikisource.org/wiki/%D7%90%D7%91%D7%9F_%D7%A2%D7%96%D7%A8%D7%90_%D7%A2%D7%9C_%D7%A7%D7%94%D7%9C%D7%AA"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:27:55.953108292Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}